<title>BELGIUM: City Bird /Swissair sign cargo de.</title>
<headline>City Bird /Swissair sign cargo de.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>City Bird, the fledgling cut price airline owned by Belgium's City Hotels, said on Wednesday it had signed a long-term cargo contract with Swissair's Swisscargo unit.</p>
<p>Under the deal, which comes into effect on March 27, Swisscargo will buy the usage of all the cargo capacity on City Bird's two MacDonald-Douglas MD-11 on their 10 regular weekly roundtrip flights from Brussels to Miami, Los Angeles, New York and Mexico City.</p>
<p>City Bird said the contract was for a minimum of 150 tonnes a week. It gave no details. - Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
